<!-- Status bar icon for the recording foreground service: the app icon's
     buildings, reduced to what survives a 24dp alpha mask.

     The earlier attempt was plain rectangles on a shared baseline, which is
     exactly the visual grammar of a bar chart. Three things pull it back to
     "building", all borrowed from appicon.svg: punched-out windows, the
     slanted roofline of the left tower (polygon54 slants up to the right),
     and the rooftop mast (polygon64).

     Windows are holes, not strokes, so they survive the alpha mask. They are
     1.8 units in a 24 viewport: ~5px at xxhdpi, ~7px at xxxhdpi, crisp. On a
     (now very rare) mdpi screen they degrade to near-solid blocks.

     Holes rely on opposite winding, NOT android:fillType="evenOdd" - fillType
     is API 24+ and this app supports 21. Outer shapes run clockwise, windows
     counter-clockwise. Keep that winding if you edit the coordinates. -->
